# Ant Design Quick Start Tutorial

## Introduction

Ant Design (antd) is a popular React UI library that provides high-quality components and design resources for building enterprise-level applications. This tutorial will help you get started with Ant Design quickly.

## Prerequisites

- Basic knowledge of React
- Node.js and npm/yarn installed
- A React project set up

## Installation

### Using npm
```bash
npm install antd
```

### Using yarn
```bash
yarn add antd
```

## Basic Setup

### 1. Import CSS
In your main application file (usually `index.js` or `App.js`), import the Ant Design CSS:

```javascript
import 'antd/dist/reset.css'; // For antd v5+
// or
import 'antd/dist/antd.css'; // For antd v4
```

### 2. Import Components
Import the components you need from antd:

```javascript
import { Button, DatePicker, Space } from 'antd';
```

## Your First Ant Design Component

Here's a simple example of using Ant Design components:

```jsx
import React from 'react';
import { Button, DatePicker, Space, Typography } from 'antd';
import 'antd/dist/reset.css';

const { Title } = Typography;

function App() {
  return (
    <div style={{ padding: '24px' }}>
      <Title level={2}>Welcome to Ant Design</Title>
      <Space direction="vertical" size="middle">
        <Button type="primary">Primary Button</Button>
        <Button>Default Button</Button>
        <Button type="dashed">Dashed Button</Button>
        <Button type="text">Text Button</Button>
        <Button type="link">Link Button</Button>

        <DatePicker placeholder="Select date" />
      </Space>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

## Common Components

### Buttons
```jsx
import { Button } from 'antd';

<Button type="primary">Primary</Button>
<Button type="default">Default</Button>
<Button type="dashed">Dashed</Button>
<Button type="text">Text</Button>
<Button type="link">Link</Button>
<Button danger>Danger</Button>
```

### Forms
```jsx
import { Form, Input, Button, Select } from 'antd';

const { Option } = Select;

function MyForm() {
  const onFinish = (values) => {
    console.log('Form values:', values);
  };

  return (
    <Form onFinish={onFinish} layout="vertical">
      <Form.Item
        label="Name"
        name="name"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please input your name!' }]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Email"
        name="email"
        rules={[
          { required: true, message: 'Please input your email!' },
          { type: 'email', message: 'Please enter a valid email!' }
        ]}
      >
        <Input />
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item
        label="Country"
        name="country"
        rules={[{ required: true, message: 'Please select your country!' }]}
      >
        <Select placeholder="Select a country">
          <Option value="china">China</Option>
          <Option value="usa">United States</Option>
          <Option value="uk">United Kingdom</Option>
        </Select>
      </Form.Item>

      <Form.Item>
        <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit">
          Submit
        </Button>
      </Form.Item>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

### Tables
```jsx
import { Table } from 'antd';

const columns = [
  {
    title: 'Name',
    dataIndex: 'name',
    key: 'name',
  },
  {
    title: 'Age',
    dataIndex: 'age',
    key: 'age',
  },
  {
    title: 'Address',
    dataIndex: 'address',
    key: 'address',
  },
];

const data = [
  {
    key: '1',
    name: 'John Brown',
    age: 32,
    address: 'New York No. 1 Lake Park',
  },
  {
    key: '2',
    name: 'Jim Green',
    age: 42,
    address: 'London No. 1 Lake Park',
  },
  {
    key: '3',
    name: 'Joe Black',
    age: 32,
    address: 'Sydney No. 1 Lake Park',
  },
];

function MyTable() {
  return <Table columns={columns} dataSource={data} />;
}
```

### Modals
```jsx
import { Modal, Button } from 'antd';
import { useState } from 'react';

function MyModal() {
  const [visible, setVisible] = useState(false);

  const showModal = () => {
    setVisible(true);
  };

  const handleOk = () => {
    setVisible(false);
  };

  const handleCancel = () => {
    setVisible(false);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <Button type="primary" onClick={showModal}>
        Open Modal
      </Button>
      <Modal
        title="Basic Modal"
        visible={visible}
        onOk={handleOk}
        onCancel={handleCancel}
      >
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
        <p>Some contents...</p>
      </Modal>
    </>
  );
}
```

## Layout Components

Ant Design provides powerful layout components:

```jsx
import { Layout, Menu, Breadcrumb } from 'antd';
import { HomeOutlined, UserOutlined, SettingOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

const { Header, Content, Footer, Sider } = Layout;

function AppLayout() {
  return (
    <Layout style={{ minHeight: '100vh' }}>
      <Sider>
        <div style={{ height: '32px', margin: '16px', background: 'rgba(255,255,255,.2)' }} />
        <Menu theme="dark" mode="inline" defaultSelectedKeys={['1']}>
          <Menu.Item key="1" icon={<HomeOutlined />}>
            Home
          </Menu.Item>
          <Menu.Item key="2" icon={<UserOutlined />}>
            User
          </Menu.Item>
          <Menu.Item key="3" icon={<SettingOutlined />}>
            Settings
          </Menu.Item>
        </Menu>
      </Sider>

      <Layout>
        <Header style={{ background: '#fff', padding: '0 16px' }} />
        <Content style={{ margin: '0 16px' }}>
          <Breadcrumb style={{ margin: '16px 0' }}>
            <Breadcrumb.Item>Home</Breadcrumb.Item>
            <Breadcrumb.Item>Dashboard</Breadcrumb.Item>
          </Breadcrumb>
          <div style={{ padding: 24, background: '#fff', minHeight: 360 }}>
            Content
          </div>
        </Content>
        <Footer style={{ textAlign: 'center' }}>
          Ant Design ©2023 Created by You
        </Footer>
      </Layout>
    </Layout>
  );
}
```

## Icons

Ant Design provides a comprehensive icon library:

```bash
npm install @ant-design/icons
```

```jsx
import { HomeOutlined, UserOutlined, SettingOutlined } from '@ant-design/icons';

<HomeOutlined />
<UserOutlined />
<SettingOutlined />
```

## Customization

### Theme Customization (v5+)
```jsx
import { ConfigProvider, theme } from 'antd';

function App() {
  return (
    <ConfigProvider
      theme={{
        algorithm: theme.darkAlgorithm,
        token: {
          colorPrimary: '#00b96b',
        },
      }}
    >
      <YourApp />
    </ConfigProvider>
  );
}
```

### Custom CSS
You can override Ant Design styles using CSS modules or styled-components:

```css
/* custom.css */
.ant-btn-primary {
  background-color: #your-color;
  border-color: #your-color;
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Import only what you need**: Use tree-shaking to reduce bundle size
2. **Use TypeScript**: Ant Design has excellent TypeScript support
3. **Follow design principles**: Stick to Ant Design's design language
4. **Responsive design**: Use Grid system for responsive layouts
5. **Accessibility**: Ant Design components are built with accessibility in mind

## Common Issues & Solutions

### CSS Import Issues
Make sure to import the CSS file before your component imports:
```javascript
import 'antd/dist/reset.css'; // Import first
import { Button } from 'antd'; // Then import components
```

### Form Validation
Always use the `rules` prop for form validation:
```jsx
<Form.Item
  rules={[
    { required: true, message: 'This field is required!' },
    { min: 3, message: 'Minimum 3 characters!' }
  ]}
>
  <Input />
</Form.Item>
```

## Resources

- [Official Documentation](https://ant.design/)
- [Component API](https://ant.design/components/overview/)
- [Design Principles](https://ant.design/docs/spec/introduce)
- [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/ant-design/ant-design)

## Next Steps

1. Explore more components in the official documentation
2. Learn about advanced features like virtual scrolling
3. Understand the design system and principles
4. Build a complete application using Ant Design

