TITLE: Update and Refresh a Session Cookie in Next.js
DESCRIPTION: The `updateSession` function illustrates how to refresh a user's session by extending its expiration date. It retrieves the current session cookie, decrypts its payload to ensure validity, and then re-sets the cookie with a new expiration time. This is useful for keeping a user logged in when they return to the application.

SOURCE: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/blob/canary/docs/01-app/02-guides/authentication.mdx#_snippet_16

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:
```
import 'server-only'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
import { decrypt } from '@/app/lib/session'

export async function updateSession() {
  const session = (await cookies()).get('session')?.value
  const payload = await decrypt(session)

  if (!session || !payload) {
    return null
  }

  const expires = new Date(Date.now() + 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000)

  const cookieStore = await cookies()
  cookieStore.set('session', session, {
    httpOnly: true,
    secure: true,
    expires: expires,
    sameSite: 'lax',
    path: '/',
  })
}
```

